# #3099 - frozen baseline for primitive identifier parameters in NON-BOUNDARY code.
#
# Format: <repo-relative path>|<permitted count>
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. The rule in PrimitiveIdParameterFenceArchitectureTests fences NEW
# `string agentId` / `string conversationId` / `string sessionId` parameters out of non-boundary
# code. At the point the rule landed the existing population was 114 declarations across 62 files;
# converting them cascades into every caller and is not reviewable as one change. Every entry below
# is therefore listed for one stated reason: it PRE-DATES the rule and is scheduled for the residual
# sweep tracked by follow-up issue #3147. No entry here is a judgement that the
# site is legitimately primitive - a site that is legitimately primitive belongs on a boundary and
# is excluded by the boundary definition, not by this list.
#
# THIS BASELINE IS SHRINK-ONLY AND IS CHECKED IN BOTH DIRECTIONS. Raising a count fails
# (a new violation landed). Leaving a count high after fixing a site ALSO fails (the entry has gone
# stale and would otherwise become a permanent licence). When you convert a site, lower or delete
# its line in the same change.
#
# Entries must stay sorted by path.
